---
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Head from '../../components/Head.astro';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <Head title="Hello, World — New Site, New Stack" description="Rebuilding prawegko.dev with Astro, deployed on S3/CloudFront with OIDC CI/CD." ogType="article" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <article class="content-container prose">
        <header class="post-header">
          <h1>Hello, World — New Site, New Stack</h1>
          <div class="post-meta">
            <time datetime="2026-09-30">September 30, 2026</time>
            <div class="tags-row">
              <span class="tag">Meta</span>
              <span class="tag">Astro</span>
              <span class="tag">AWS</span>
              <span class="tag">Cloud</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </header>

        <p>Welcome to the new prawegko.dev. This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, a modern static site generator that produces fast, lightweight websites by default.</p>

        <h2>Why Astro?</h2>
        <p>After running on NextJS + Vercel for a while, I wanted to try a different deployment approach:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Static by default</strong> — Astro ships zero JavaScript unless you need it</li>
          <li><strong>Content Collections</strong> — native MDX support with typed frontmatter</li>
          <li><strong>Cloud-native deployment</strong> — S3 + CloudFront with OIDC-based GitHub Actions CI/CD</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>The Stack</h2>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Choice</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Framework</td><td>Astro 7 + TypeScript</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Styling</td><td>CSS custom properties</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hosting</td><td>AWS S3 (prawegko.dev bucket)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>CDN</td><td>CloudFront</td></tr>
          <tr><td>CI/CD</td><td>GitHub Actions with OIDC role deploy</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Domain</td><td>prawegko.dev via Route53</td></tr>
        </table>

        <h2>The Workflow</h2>
        <pre><code>git push origin main
  -> npm ci
  -> npm run build
  -> aws s3 sync dist/ s3://prawegko.dev --delete
  -> aws cloudfront create-invalidation ...</code></pre>
        <p>All authenticated through GitHub's OIDC provider — no long-lived AWS keys needed.</p>
        <p>More posts coming soon. Stay tuned.</p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<script>
(function() {
  const html = document.documentElement;
  const stored = localStorage.getItem('theme');
  if (stored === 'light' || stored === 'dark') {
    html.setAttribute('data-theme', stored);
  }
})();
</script>

<style>
  .post-header { margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); }
  .post-header h1 { font-size: var(--font-size-3xl); font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .post-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-sm); margin-top: var(--space-md); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .post-meta time { font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .tags-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-xs); }
</style>